{"kind":"request","text":"S4: choose the missing Question-to-Brief binding\n\nThe literal S4 witness requires the Brief bytes' digest to equal a digest pinned by the question. Main c8c7b631 has no such relation: issue-questions.ts:15–27 stores the question body and bodyAt; ask fields at50–54 have no Brief field. ViewResources at resources.ts:35–55 accepts ui:// HTML only. The question-body digest is a different value and cannot stand in for the Brief. Both the inventory owner and independent Source review confirmed these facts.\n\nA concrete Source-only proposal is /private/tmp/artroom-s4-brief-binding-proposal-20261031-v1/PROPOSAL.md, SHA256 47e986d05dcefad9af74824e8e682d066eb8f216a2aac7737c0c149525e3a85b; its source index is 6ac71556a959204f8083e6439f71041e631989c62346bc7df9f77c4aea1eeaa0. Two choices are reviewable:\n\nA. Keep S4 strictly read-only. Bind full question scope/item/bodyAt to an immutable operator-trusted package-context table. Amend the witness to package-pinned context, since the native question would still own no Brief pin.\n\nB. Preserve the literal question-pinned witness. Adopt a new opt-in S3-derived definition with one fixed required ask value/field brief using the existing digest form, stored by ask. Preserve every old S3 byte and pin, all existing bodyAt/person-only approval semantics and all act names. The Brief stays immutable for that question; a different Brief requires a new question. Legacy questions remain explicitly unbound. This declared-data addition needs your scope amendment because S4 currently promises reads and one view.\n\nI recommend B if the literal witness stands. In either case, adopt a separate bounded text/plain resource at dap://package/brief, with exact raw UTF-8 bytes and digestBytes verification. Proposed bound:64KiB. Preserve the HTML ui:// MIME/CSP/digest owner; add no generic URI loader, external fetch, executable package body or body-digest fallback. The pin grants no native authority and does not turn question approval into approval of the Brief or conditions.\n\nPlease decide A or B, whether the Brief is immutable across question text revisions, and the proposed text-resource bound. No pin, definition, act or resource implementation has been fabricated or changed for this proposal. S2's first required inventory is committed separately at ace70362, and its unaffected kit work can continue. V12 initialization request5fbd205c remains the execution priority; its result is still awaited.","body":{"conditions":"Adopt the concrete question/Brief binding and immutable-revision policy, or amend the witness to package-pinned context; decide the bounded plain-text resource. No runtime action or old profile rewrite is authorized by this question alone.","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f15b9b44c018b1e345b3efe558fcee29d26bffb0 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}